// syslUI — a declarative retained user interface for a machine with a heap.
//
//     dependencies {
//       syslui { git = "github.com/sysl-lang/syslui", version = "0.1.10" }
//     }
//
// **The presentation is not in here.** What the toolkit produces is a block of premultiplied ARGB32
// pixels; a window, a frame loop and events are `sysl-lang/syslui-sdl`, which is a separate package
// because a link directive is never pruned and SDL3 has no business on the link line of a program
// that draws into a panel.
//
// It began as the probe card 0203 asks for, and the six questions it asks about the architecture
// decided in 0168 are answered. What is here now is a styling layer built on those answers:
// chainable modifiers, a view whose appearance is decided while it is drawn, and animation. The API
// is still moving.
//
// `imui` is the sibling for a panel on a microcontroller and is not replaced by this: it refuses a
// retained tree on purpose, and the split between the two is by application size rather than by
// device.

package {
  name    = "syslui"
  version = "0.1.10"

  // **The oldest compiler this builds with is 0.7.7, the one it was last built and tested with.** This
  // package's own source asks for less: an
  // indented block tree (`column(spacing = 8):`), `Size` and `Rect` writing their own `Eq`, `sysl.seq`,
  // the **leading-dot call chain** that `style.sysl` breaks a modifier chain with, and a default
  // naming a type parameter (`step: T = T.zero()`). The floor is the dependency's: `plutovg` 0.2.6
  // imports `sysl.raw` and calls `.to_string()`, neither of which exists on 0.5.x, and a consumer
  // of this package builds `plutovg` with it.
  sysl = "0.7.7"
}

// The drawing backend, and the one dependency.
//
// **PlutoVG is here because of corners.** SDL3 has no shape or path API, and the triangle fan that
// would draw a rounded rectangle is not antialiased — while a rounded *border* is an annulus, which
// is not convex and cannot be drawn that way at all. PlutoVG vendors FreeType's `ftgrays`
// rasterizer, carries its own C, and needs nothing installed, which is why the same backend serves
// a desktop and a phone.
dependencies {
  plutovg { git = "github.com/sysl-lang/plutovg", version = "0.2.6" }
}

// **An erased tree is boxes, so `heap` is not negotiable** — that is the bargain 0168 struck against
// `imui`'s, and it was the whole of what this package asked for while the only backend was a
// recorder that drew nothing.
//
// **`posix` arrived with PlutoVG and is narrower than it looks**: in that package it is `write_png`
// and loading a face from a *file*, and nothing else — a program that renders into a buffer it owns
// and loads its font from bytes linked into the binary touches no operating system. It is declared
// because a capability is a property of the module rather than of the call.
requires {
  heap  = true
  posix = true
}
